Features:
---------

        Our assignment comes with these bonus features:
        We implemented the following primitives usiing our ray tracer
                - sphere
                - plane
                - square
                - triangle
        We also implemented the following thing you can change for each object
                - ambient light
                - diffuse
                - specular
                - filter
                - transmit 
                - reflect
                - ior
                - caustic
        What you see in the GL window is what you get plus a plane.  
        Our ray tracer uses a script language that we developed so the ray tracer 
        is independent of Lab 2


How to run:
-----------
        in the lab2 directory
	        type make
	in the lab3 directory 
                type make (this makes the ray tracer program)
        
        type ./lab2  in the lab2 directory

Scripts
-------
        See the example scripts called example1 or train too see how a script works.
 
        Running a script
        in the lab 3 directory type
                ./rt script_file_name | xv -


Lab 2 addons 
------------


Open file:
----------
	Use File -> Open to open the sample programs called:
		sample1 sample2 example1 example2 clown

Saving a file
-------------
	Use File -> Save to save the current list to a file

Exporting a file
----------------
        Use File -> Export to convert your current opengl window to a raytraced one

Creating a list
---------------	
	On runing ./lab1 a QTwindow apears called "Control Window".
	
	Adding a Node.
		Use the Add button to add a node to the right of the
		current Node you are at in the list.
	
	Deleting a Node
		Use the Delete button to delete the current node you are
		at. 
	
	Naming a Node
		Use the Name: edit box to enter the name of the current
		node u are at.
		
	Node ID.
		The Node ID is read only and is set when the add command
		is used 

	Matrix Frame
		The Matrix frame contains an editable 4x4 matrix all
		elemnets of the matrix can be edited. As the nodes are
		traversed the matrix changes.
		
		Load Identity button
			This button loads the identity matrix into the current
			matrix.	
	
	Matrix Controls Frame
		The matrix Control frame contains transforms that
		automaticly updates the current matrix.
		
		Add Rotate Button
			This button add a rotation of degree X  to the
			current Matrix.  User enters data in degrees.
                        The first box is for x second for y, and third for z.

		Add Xlat. Button
			This Button adds a translation in the x,y
			direction to thecurrent matrix.   
                        The first box is for x second for y, and third for z.
		
		Add Scale Button
			This Button adds a Scaling Factor in the x,y
			direction to the current matrix.  
                        The first box is for x second for y, and third for z.
		
		Add Shear Button
			This Button adds a Shearing Factor in the x,y
                        direction to the current matrix.  
                        The first box is for x second for y, and third for z.

	Recursion Frame
		Link to: Edit Box
			This edit box is used to specife the name of the
			Node the current node is to be linked to. 		
 		
		Count: Edit Box
			This edit box is used to specify the number of
			time the two nodes should be called in recursion.

	        
         Primitive frame       
                Primitive
                Use the drop down box to select the primitive the current node will point to.

	        The second drop down alows the folloing to be set for each primitive
                        - ambient light                                                                 0 <= x <= 1
                        - diffuse                                                                       0 <= x <= 1
                        - specular                                                                      0 <= x <= 1
                        - filter        This makes the object filter light                              0 <= x <= 1
                        - transmit      This makes the object transmit light                            0 <= x <= 1
                        - reflect       this makes the object reflect light                             0 <= x <= 1
                        - ior           index of refraction                                             0 <= x <= 1
                        - caustic       causes a spher to have a piont of light in the filtered shadow  0 <= x <= 1
                Color        
                The first box is for red second for green, and third for blue.
                

        GLWindow at bottom of window

		This window shows the current linked list.  It can be
		navigated using the left mouse button then moving the mouse, or by using
		the buttons on either side of the window	 

        Show Axes
                Turns the Axes on or off for the current node
                This feature has been removed
        No perspective
                Turns perspective view on or off
                this feature has been removed
        Recursion
                Turns recursion on or off




Lab 2 window
	
	This window shows the 3D output of the link list.
        
        Mouse
                Use the mouse to rotate, zoom, translate the object in 3d
        
        Holding shift then moving the mouse moves the light source






